    "definitions": {
      "short": "cunning (usually in a bad sense)",
      "usage": "crafty, prudent, subtil.",
      "full": "H6175. arum עָרוּם adjective crafty, shrewd, sensible ; — 1 crafty , ׳ע as predicate, of serpent Gen 3:1 ; plural as substantive עֲרוּמִים מַחְשְׁבוֺת Job 5:12 , ע ׳לְשׁוֺן 15:5 . 2 in Proverbs, in good sense (opposed to מֶּתִי כְּסִיל, אֱוִיל, ); as attributive עָרוּם אָדָם Prov 12:23 a shrewd or sensible man ; ׳ע as substantive = id. , 12:16 ; 13:16 , so ע ׳חָכְמַת 13:8 ; = prudent man 14:15 ; 22:3 ; 27:12 ; plural עֲרוּמִים 14:18 . עֵרָנִי עֵרָן, see below I. עור . ערס (√ of following).",
